<td id="S3.T1.2.1.10.15" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.T1.2.1.10.15.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">70.82</span></td>
<td id="S3.T1.2.1.10.16" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.T1.2.1.10.16.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">55.47</span></td>
<td id="S3.T1.2.1.10.17" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.T1.2.1.10.17.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">68.68</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
<figure id="S3.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>Performance of RepoFormer-3B on ReccEval (Use 100% data for evaluation). <math id="S3.T2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>: only use left context.</figcaption>
<div id="S3.T2.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:166.4pt;height:39.4pt;vertical-align:-17.7pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-20.8pt,4.9pt) scale(0.8,0.8) ;">
<table id="S3.T2.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S3.T2.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="S3.T2.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Dataset</span></td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" colspan="4">RepoFormer-3B</td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T2.2.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T2.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_td"></td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" colspan="2">Code Match</td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" colspan="2">Identifier Match</td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T2.2.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T2.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_td"></td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">EM</td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">ES</td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.1.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">EM</td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.1.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">F1</td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T2.2.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T2.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">ReccEval<sub id="S3.T2.2.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_sub"><span id="S3.T2.2.1.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">l</span></sub></td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">12.88</td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.1.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">48.21</td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.1.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">19.81</td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.1.4.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">36.93</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first report the results when using all ReccEval data for evaluation in Tab. <a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 3.2.1 Overall Performance ‣ 3.2 Evaluation Results 17 footnote 17 17 footnote 17 The results for CCEval are reported in Appendix . ‣ 3 Experiment ‣ CodeRAG: Finding Relevant and Necessary Knowledge for Retrieval-Augmented Repository-Level Code Completion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and Tab. <a href="#S3.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 3.2.1 Overall Performance ‣ 3.2 Evaluation Results 17 footnote 17 17 footnote 17 The results for CCEval are reported in Appendix . ‣ 3 Experiment ‣ CodeRAG: Finding Relevant and Necessary Knowledge for Retrieval-Augmented Repository-Level Code Completion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, as done in existing works.
In this case, LLM reranker (i.e., <math id="S3.SS2.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{CodeRAG}_{\text{llmr}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>CodeRAG</mtext><mtext>llmr</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{CodeRAG}_{\text{llmr}}</annotation></semantics></math>) is used instead of distilled reranker (i.e., <math id="S3.SS2.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{CodeRAG}_{\text{disr}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>CodeRAG</mtext><mtext>disr</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{CodeRAG}_{\text{disr}}</annotation></semantics></math>) since distilled reranker requires training data.
The results of splitting ReccEval for training and evaluating the distilled reranker are analyzed in Sec. <a href="#S3.SS2.SSS3" title="3.2.3 Comparisons between LLM Reranker and Distilled Reranker ‣ 3.2 Evaluation Results 17 footnote 17 17 footnote 17 The results for CCEval are reported in Appendix . ‣ 3 Experiment ‣ CodeRAG: Finding Relevant and Necessary Knowledge for Retrieval-Augmented Repository-Level Code Completion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2.3</span></a>.
From Tab. <a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 3.2.1 Overall Performance ‣ 3.2 Evaluation Results 17 footnote 17 17 footnote 17 The results for CCEval are reported in Appendix . ‣ 3 Experiment ‣ CodeRAG: Finding Relevant and Necessary Knowledge for Retrieval-Augmented Repository-Level Code Completion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and Tab. <a href="#S3.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 3.2.1 Overall Performance ‣ 3.2 Evaluation Results 17 footnote 17 17 footnote 17 The results for CCEval are reported in Appendix . ‣ 3 Experiment ‣ CodeRAG: Finding Relevant and Necessary Knowledge for Retrieval-Augmented Repository-Level Code Completion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, we have the following observations:</p>
<ul id="S3.I4" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:10pt;">
<li id="S3.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">It is clear that Zero-Shot has the worst performance across all settings, showing that solely relying on code LLMs cannot provide satisfying repository-level code completion.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">CCFinder and RG-1 show significant improvements over Zero-Shot but they are outperformed by more sophisticated approaches. The results indicate that RAG indeed enhances code completion but the improvements are limited since general RAG techniques are not tailored to repository-level code completion.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">RepoCoder consistently outperforms CCFinder and RG-1, demonstrating that iterative retrieval <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shao et al. (2023)</a></cite> exceeds naive RAG in code completion.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I4.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">DraCo and RepoFuse show competitive performance and they show much better results than other baselines when larger code LLMs are used, showing that larger code LLMs may better understand the data dependence features.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I4.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Comparing Tab. <a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 3.2.1 Overall Performance ‣ 3.2 Evaluation Results 17 footnote 17 17 footnote 17 The results for CCEval are reported in Appendix . ‣ 3 Experiment ‣ CodeRAG: Finding Relevant and Necessary Knowledge for Retrieval-Augmented Repository-Level Code Completion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and Tab. <a href="#S3.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 3.2.1 Overall Performance ‣ 3.2 Evaluation Results 17 footnote 17 17 footnote 17 The results for CCEval are reported in Appendix . ‣ 3 Experiment ‣ CodeRAG: Finding Relevant and Necessary Knowledge for Retrieval-Augmented Repository-Level Code Completion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, we can find that RepoFormer-3B using only left context lags behind other methods except Zero-Shot.
The possible reason is that RepoFormer-3B is optimized to consider both left and right contexts for code completion while other baselines and <span id="S3.I4.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">CodeRAG</span> are designed to consider only the left context.
On ReccEval, where the right context is unavailable, the performance of RepoFormer-3B significantly degrades.
We provide the results of RepoFormer-3B on CCEval, where both left and right contexts are available, in Tab. <a href="#A1.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ Appendix A Results on CCEval ‣ CodeRAG: Finding Relevant and Necessary Knowledge for Retrieval-Augmented Repository-Level Code Completion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> of Appendix <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Results on CCEval ‣ CodeRAG: Finding Relevant and Necessary Knowledge for Retrieval-Augmented Repository-Level Code Completion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I4.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I4.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">CodeRAG</span> achieves the best performance across all settings on ReccEval, showing its effectiveness.
Besides, the performance gains over baselines consistently exist as the size of code LLM increases, showing the robustness of <span id="S3.I4.i6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text">CodeRAG</span>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">3.2.2 </span>Ablation Study</h4>

