</figure>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To investigate whether each part in <span id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">CodeRAG</span> indeed contributes to its performance, we compare <span id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text">CodeRAG</span> with its variations on ReccEval using 100% data for evaluation.
The results are reported in Tab. <a href="#S3.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 3.2.2 Ablation Study ‣ 3.2 Evaluation Results 17 footnote 17 17 footnote 17 The results for CCEval are reported in Appendix . ‣ 3 Experiment ‣ CodeRAG: Finding Relevant and Necessary Knowledge for Retrieval-Augmented Repository-Level Code Completion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.
Subscripts “df”, “s”, “d” and “lr” indicate using dataflow-guided retrieval, using sparse retrieval, using dense retrieval and using LLM reranker, respectively.
In other words, <math id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{CodeRAG}_{\text{df+s+d+lr}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>CodeRAG</mtext><mtext>df+s+d+lr</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{CodeRAG}_{\text{df+s+d+lr}}</annotation></semantics></math> is identical to <math id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{CodeRAG}_{\text{llmr}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>CodeRAG</mtext><mtext>llmr</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{CodeRAG}_{\text{llmr}}</annotation></semantics></math> shown in Tab. <a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 3.2.1 Overall Performance ‣ 3.2 Evaluation Results 17 footnote 17 17 footnote 17 The results for CCEval are reported in Appendix . ‣ 3 Experiment ‣ CodeRAG: Finding Relevant and Necessary Knowledge for Retrieval-Augmented Repository-Level Code Completion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">From the results, we can observe that incorporating more retrieval paths brings improvements to code completion in most cases.
Besides, using reranking module can significantly boost performance.
These findings highlight the effectiveness of multi-path code retrieval and applying reranking in improving repository-level code completion.</p>
</div>
</section>
