</figure>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We further compare the results of using LLM reranker (<math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{CodeRAG}_{\text{llmr}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>CodeRAG</mtext><mtext>llmr</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{CodeRAG}_{\text{llmr}}</annotation></semantics></math>) and using distilled reranker (<math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{CodeRAG}_{\text{disr}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>CodeRAG</mtext><mtext>disr</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{CodeRAG}_{\text{disr}}</annotation></semantics></math>) on ReccEval in Tab. <a href="#S3.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 3.2.3 Comparisons between LLM Reranker and Distilled Reranker ‣ 3.2 Evaluation Results 17 footnote 17 17 footnote 17 The results for CCEval are reported in Appendix . ‣ 3 Experiment ‣ CodeRAG: Finding Relevant and Necessary Knowledge for Retrieval-Augmented Repository-Level Code Completion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.
As <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{CodeRAG}_{\text{disr}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>CodeRAG</mtext><mtext>disr</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{CodeRAG}_{\text{disr}}</annotation></semantics></math> requires training, we randomly sample 70% data for training and the remaining 30% data is used for testing.
The results in Tab. <a href="#S3.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 3.2.3 Comparisons between LLM Reranker and Distilled Reranker ‣ 3.2 Evaluation Results 17 footnote 17 17 footnote 17 The results for CCEval are reported in Appendix . ‣ 3 Experiment ‣ CodeRAG: Finding Relevant and Necessary Knowledge for Retrieval-Augmented Repository-Level Code Completion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> are reported over the test data.
From the results, we can observe that using the distilled reranker affects the performance compared to using LLM reranker, but the performance is still competitive.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">3.2.4 </span>Comparisons among Different Retrieval Query Construction Methods.</h4>

