<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Results on CCEval</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In addition to ReccEval, we also conduct experiments on the CCEval benchmark.
Tab. <a href="#A1.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ Appendix A Results on CCEval ‣ CodeRAG: Finding Relevant and Necessary Knowledge for Retrieval-Augmented Repository-Level Code Completion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> reports the results on CCEval using LLM reranker in <span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">CodeRAG</span> and 100% data for evaluation.
Tab. <a href="#A1.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ Appendix A Results on CCEval ‣ CodeRAG: Finding Relevant and Necessary Knowledge for Retrieval-Augmented Repository-Level Code Completion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> provides the results on CCEval using distilled reranker in <span id="A1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text">CodeRAG</span> and 30% data for evaluation.
Tab. <a href="#A1.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ Appendix A Results on CCEval ‣ CodeRAG: Finding Relevant and Necessary Knowledge for Retrieval-Augmented Repository-Level Code Completion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> shows the results using Repoformer-3B with RG-1 as the retriever on CCEval.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">From Tab. <a href="#A1.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ Appendix A Results on CCEval ‣ CodeRAG: Finding Relevant and Necessary Knowledge for Retrieval-Augmented Repository-Level Code Completion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> and Tab. <a href="#A1.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ Appendix A Results on CCEval ‣ CodeRAG: Finding Relevant and Necessary Knowledge for Retrieval-Augmented Repository-Level Code Completion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>, we can see similar trends as observed on ReccEval.
From Tab. <a href="#A1.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ Appendix A Results on CCEval ‣ CodeRAG: Finding Relevant and Necessary Knowledge for Retrieval-Augmented Repository-Level Code Completion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>, we can observe that the performance of Repoformer-3B using both left and right contexts gets significantly improved compared to Repoformer-3B using only left context since it is optimized to use left and right parts of the cursor position.
By comparing <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{CodeRAG}_{\text{llmr}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>CodeRAG</mtext><mtext>llmr</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{CodeRAG}_{\text{llmr}}</annotation></semantics></math> with StarCoder2-3B in Tab. <a href="#A1.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ Appendix A Results on CCEval ‣ CodeRAG: Finding Relevant and Necessary Knowledge for Retrieval-Augmented Repository-Level Code Completion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> and Repoformer-3B in Tab. <a href="#A1.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ Appendix A Results on CCEval ‣ CodeRAG: Finding Relevant and Necessary Knowledge for Retrieval-Augmented Repository-Level Code Completion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>, we can observe that <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{CodeRAG}_{\text{llmr}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>CodeRAG</mtext><mtext>llmr</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{CodeRAG}_{\text{llmr}}</annotation></semantics></math> which only considers left context outperforms Repoformer-3B that uses both left and right contexts, when 3B code LLM is used as code generator, showing the effectiveness of <span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">CodeRAG</span>.</p>
</div>
